ExhibitOS documentation licensing

This file defines the scope of the unmodified license texts in LICENSES/.

Project-owned prose and diagrams in Markdown documentation, including README.md
and AGENTS.md, are licensed under CC-BY-4.0. See LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt.
Use attribution: ExhibitOS contributors, the original document URL, a link to
CC-BY-4.0, and an indication of changes when sharing adapted documentation.
Retain supplied author, copyright and disclaimer information.

Executable examples in fenced code blocks and project-owned source, configuration,
build and verification scripts are licensed under Apache-2.0. This code exception
takes precedence over the surrounding documentation license.
See LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt. Retain relevant copyright and attribution notices,
provide the license, indicate modified files, and carry required upstream NOTICEs.

Third-party quotations, code, media, dependencies and their notices retain their
original terms. Explicit per-file notices override this default mapping.
LICENSES/*.txt are unmodified legal texts and are not relicensed as project prose.

These licenses do not grant trademark rights or change the rights in imported
artworks or personal data. This repository contains no such artwork assets today.
Review rights and record provenance before adding them.

Official source texts:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode.txt
https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.txt
